<title>USA: U.S. reviewing EU gene label proposal - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. reviewing EU gene label proposal - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. is still trying to gather information about a new European Union proposal on labelling genetically modified foods, a senior U.S. Agriculture Department official said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We need to get more information. We don't have enough to react either favorably or unfavorably,&quot; said Paul Drazek, U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman's trade adviser.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the European Commission agreed on guidelines on labelling of products produced from genetically modified organisms (GMOs). It said it would use these guidelines to prepare draft legislation after the summer break.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a decision to do something but they have not developed anything on paper yet to our knowledge,&quot; said Drazek. &quot;The proof will be in the pudding.&quot;</p>
<p>The USDA trade adviser said the U.S. hoped to get more information before Europe shut down next week for the summer.</p>
